    <info>
        <p>This page contains guidelines for depositors regarding file formats suitable for long-term preservation in the <a href="https://repository.clarin.hr/">HR-CLARIN repository</a>.</p>
        <p>
            File formats are classified into three acceptance levels across multiple domains. These levels are defined as follows: 
            “recommended” means that the file format is suitable for long-term data preservation within a given domain; 
            “acceptable” means that there are formats more suitable for long-term preservation that depositors might consider; 
            and “discouraged” means that the format, although sometimes used within a certain domain, is not suitable for depositing.
        </p>
        <p>This list is not exhaustive and is subject to revision. Depositors are welcome to contact <a href="mailto:clarin@clarin.hr">HR-CLARIN</a> with any questions.</p>
    </info>
